an></b></div></th></tr><tr><th><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><b><span style="direction:ltr;">Consistency &nbsp;<br></span></b></div><ul style="margin-left:32px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· The <b><span style="direction:ltr;">correct referencing style</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> <span style="direction:ltr;">for the <b><span style="direction:ltr;">discipline </span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">â€“ i.e., either <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Harvard</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">, OR <b><span style="direction:ltr;">APA</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> (for <span style="direction:ltr;">Psychology)<b><span style="direction:ltr;">,</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> OR <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Law</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">, OR<b><span style="direction:ltr;"> IEEE </span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">(for ICT/Engineering) â€“ has <span style="direction:ltr;">been used consistently for all <span style="direction:ltr;">in-text references and in the <span style="direction:ltr;">bibliography/reference list. <br></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div><ul style="margin-left:32px;"><li><div style="direction:ltr;"><span style="direction:ltr;">Â· <b><span style="direction:ltr;">Concepts</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> and<b><span style="direction:ltr;"> ideas</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> that are <b><span style="direction:ltr;">quoted</span></b><span style="direction:ltr;"> and/or <b><span style="direction:ltr;">paraphrased </span></b><span style="direction:ltr;">are referenced consistently <span style="direction:ltr;">throughout. <br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></li></ul><div style="direction:ltr;margin-top:5px"><span style="direction:ltr;"> <br></span></div><ul style="margin-lef